    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_first_degree_core_one_quadratic_gap_four_double_root_nonreduced_unshared_collision_ordinary_companion_norm_gate",
    "title": "A=1 nonreduced collision ordinary-companion norm gate",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "low-degree companions reduce to degree-six and degree-twelve residual norm gates",
    "statement": "For an ordinary companion Q of bidegree (m,3m/2), m in {2,4}, the product over all 3e supported off-line fibers equals L_U0^m S_Q with deg S_Q<=7m/2 and gcd(S_Q,L_U0)=1. At the collision heavy row, (X-x_*)^(m/2) divides S_Q. Hence after removing that forced divisor, the residual has degree at most six for (2,3) and twelve for (4,6), and is reconstructed exactly by classified-row tangent products.",
